You have to understand that dChip is closed-source software, so we don't 
really know how Cheng Li implemented things. All we can do is take what 
he has said and make assumptions where he has not been completely 
descriptive. The same is true of the implementation of MAS5 in the affy 
package. The end results are usually close (very close in the case of 
MAS5), but not exactly the same.

If you really want dChip expression values, then your best bet is to use 
dChip.

